\title[The positional/magnitude stratum of the barrier-4 converse]
{The Positional/Magnitude Stratum of the Barrier-4 Converse:\\
Certified Silence, Adaptive Saturation, and a Strict SET/COST Dichotomy}

\author{Aristotle}
\date{29 August 2026}

\begin{abstract}
We develop a complete cost calculus for hint-assisted search, in the min-plus (``tropical'')
setting used to study factor location on the divisor hyperbola $X \odot Y = N$.
In the \emph{fixed-window} stratum we prove that the correct law for a committed oracle protocol is
the certified-silence law $S_A(\mu,P) = 1/[\mu P + (1-P)(1-\mu)]$, which strictly supersedes the
fire-or-silent law $1/(1-(1-\mu)P)$; that the certified law, the fire-or-silent law and the
re-scan protocol $S_B = 1/(1+\mu-P)$ lie in arithmetic progression with common gap $\mu(1-P)$; that
block-first ordering dominates unconditionally for the certified protocol but \emph{iff} $\mu \le P$
for the re-scan protocol; that the cap $S_A \le 1/\mu$ is valid only for $\mu \le 1/2$, the honest
bound being $1/\min(\mu,1-\mu)$; that at $\mu = 1/2$ the certified cost is $1/2$ for every $P$; and
that no constant caps $S_A$. In the \emph{adaptive} stratum we prove exact saturation
$\cost(2^m,m) = \log_2 W + \tfrac12$ as the fixed point of $V(2W)=V(W)+1$, $V(1)=\tfrac12$; the exact
net marginal identity $\cost(k)-\cost(k+1) = W/2^{k+2}-1$ together with the refutation of its gross
form; the separation of the pin from the argmin by exactly half a query, with the argmin attained on
a two-point plateau at offsets $\{-2,-1\}$; and the bracket
$\log_2 W - \tfrac12 \le \min_k \cost(W,k) \le \log_2 W + \tfrac12$ for $W \ge 1$. In the
\emph{dichotomy} stratum we prove that pipeline speedups factor, $S(R\circ F)=S(R)S(F)$; that
$4/3$ is a \emph{greatest} element of the residue (COST-class) speedups, attained exactly at density
$\theta = 1/2$, and that it is the extremum of the uninformative diagonal $P=\mu$ of the
fixed-window surface; and that the positional (SET-class) factor obeys a Cauchy--Schwarz bits cap
$S(R) \le n \le 2^k$ attained exactly at uniform partitions. Four measured anchors are exact
rationals $400/77$, $200000/28943$, $200000/45986$, $500000/17203$; all exceed $4/3$ yet factor
legally, so exceeding the residue cap is \emph{class-crossing}, not cap-breaking. At the corner
window $[1,\sqrt N]$ of the divisor hyperbola, where a semiprime $N=pq$ has exactly one nontrivial
witness, any pipeline built from a positional stage of cost at least $1/\sqrt N$ and an arbitrary
residue filter has speedup at most $\tfrac43 \sqrt N$: residue sieving buys a constant, never an
exponent.
\end{abstract}

